I've now traced the full content pipeline. The key findings:

1. **`src/services/contentstack.ts`** — The `contentstack.Stack(options)` initialization at line 69 uses `options` (lines 55-67) that lacks any `live_preview` configuration. This is the CAUSE — the Contentstack SDK's live preview feature is never enabled at the Stack level.

2. **`src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx`** — The `ContentstackProvider` only accepts static `defaultContent` and has no mechanism to receive/merge live preview data from the SDK.

The Stack options object is where Contentstack Live Preview must be enabled — without it, the SDK never participates in the preview protocol regardless of what the client does.

